cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8360396Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8370185Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8486539Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8498640Z ^[[0m
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8499569Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8500257Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8500577Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8500927Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8501601Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8501962Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8502932Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8503560Z    if you are ready to continue.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8503850Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8504394Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8505469Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8506071Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8506537Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8506919Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8507519Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8507838Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8508112Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8508816Z    can use Nix.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8509024Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8509216Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8509473Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8509951Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8510799Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8512709Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8513026Z I will:
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8513404Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8513871Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8514560Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8515089Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8515780Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8516189Z  - install Nix in /nix
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8516659Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8517755Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8518288Z    /root
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8531687Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8532836Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8545265Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8546061Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8546545Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8552573Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8553583Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8572601Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8574129Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8586469Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8587828Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8588501Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8588914Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8589404Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8589701Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8589975Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8590547Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8590842Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8591194Z If you would like to
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8591585Z see the output, try like this:
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8591969Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8592245Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8592803Z   $ sh ./install-nix
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8593030Z 
cli (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.8593044Z 
