check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2392805Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2401519Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2498768Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2509702Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2510624Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2511316Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2511581Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2511847Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2512525Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2512903Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2513660Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2514177Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2514509Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2515032Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2515976Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2516654Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2517100Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2517309Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2517585Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2517957Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2518403Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2518855Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2519019Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2519257Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2519484Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2519912Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2520468Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2520794Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2520975Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2521248Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2521539Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2522150Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2522646Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2523075Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2523482Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2523805Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2524327Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2524757Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2537076Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2538671Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2547384Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2548276Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2548630Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2551765Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2552352Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2567953Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2568638Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2578219Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2578912Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2583961Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2584241Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2584469Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2584712Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2585146Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2585612Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2585853Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:27.2586023Z If you would like to
