conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9019629Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9027036Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9124183Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9134122Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9135843Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9136776Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9137122Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9137431Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9138128Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9138538Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9139264Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9139913Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9140325Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9140902Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9141980Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9142684Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9143186Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9143456Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9143781Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9144230Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9144895Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9145472Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9145710Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9146043Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9146325Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9146835Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9147479Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9147928Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9148223Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9148553Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9148806Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9149449Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9150029Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9150614Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9151095Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9151507Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9152129Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9152746Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9160953Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9162061Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9172741Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9173686Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9175863Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9176415Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9176994Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9193563Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9194671Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9203990Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9205393Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9206496Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9206834Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9207197Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9207619Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9207890Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9208467Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9208825Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9209130Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9209604Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9209872Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9210157Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9210807Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.9211063Z 
