conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4111127Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4121952Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4227073Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4237263Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4238120Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4239052Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4239791Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4240254Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4241292Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4241875Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4242758Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4243650Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4244038Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4244726Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4245655Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4246237Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4246675Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4246891Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4247206Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4247517Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4247770Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4248230Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4248436Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4248570Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4248776Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4249109Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4249970Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4250423Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4250679Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4251041Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4251469Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4252308Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4253169Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4253962Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4254550Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4255077Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4255597Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4256125Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4266741Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4267685Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4278927Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4280015Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4280613Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4281885Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4282730Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4301566Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4302325Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4312993Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4313858Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4314748Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4315211Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4315578Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4316090Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4316519Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4317411Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:26.4317878Z 
