check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.7886328Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.7900824Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8039287Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8049947Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8050863Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8051748Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8052160Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8052530Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8053387Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8053916Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8054664Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8055134Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8056022Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8056553Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8057548Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8058021Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8058416Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8058598Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8058820Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8059090Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8059315Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8059709Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8060072Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8060244Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8060475Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8060815Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8061535Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8061940Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8062103Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8062301Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8062617Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8063303Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8063985Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8064395Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8064706Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8065013Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8065481Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8066588Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8078359Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8079296Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8088583Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8089517Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8090136Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8090743Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:25.8091372Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
