conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5309615Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5384615Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5393818Z ^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5394347Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5394969Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5395266Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5395556Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5396174Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5396553Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5396809Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5397324Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5397999Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5398836Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5399970Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5400680Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5401146Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5401402Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5401693Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5402025Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5402300Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5402788Z    can use Nix.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5402990Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5403138Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5403372Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5403749Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5404348Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5406713Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5406905Z I will:
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5407167Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5407436Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5407978Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5408726Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5409231Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5409600Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5409970Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5410495Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5410821Z    /root
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:31.5419003Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
